  "reproduction": "Before the fix all four original desktop DM/group cases failed: first-frame positioning remained thousands of pixels above the end, and sending while reading history did not restore the end position.",
  "test_iterations": [
    "The expanded group-queue fixture initially let responder routing fail instead of creating queued work. It now addresses its fixture agent explicitly; desktop/mobile and WebKit reruns pass.",
    "One WebKit case initially exceeded the five-second initial-data wait under concurrent compilation/browser load. The initial-data wait is now 15 seconds; its isolated rerun passes. The first-frame and bottom-position assertions remain unchanged."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Browser cases use real HTTP/application persistence and controlled public timeline fixtures.",
    "WebKit is browser-engine coverage; this follow-up did not automate clicks in a native Tauri window.",
    "The desktop package was rebuilt, but a running older process must be quit before opening the updated bundle."
